From 061c3dd056f7b81ff40bdc8cb964d56b755395f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 22:36:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] v4.6: fix llist CPU mismatch -- this_cpu_ptr -> &per_cpu(...,
 cpu_of(rq))

The restoration trigger in enqueue_task_fair used this_cpu_ptr() to
select the llist head, but queue_balance_callback used cpu_of(rq).
During a cross-CPU wakeup (e.g., try_to_wake_up on CPU A waking a task
destined for CPU B), these point to different CPUs.  The llist node
was added to CPU A's list but the worker only drained CPU B's list.

Kill chain (confirmed by review-007):
1. Plymouth (initramfs) runs SCHED_FIFO, exceeds 9.5ms rt_ema
2. Safety valve demotes it to SCHED_NORMAL
3. Plymouth sleeps/wakes across CPUs; restoration node stranded
4. Plymouth exits -> task_struct freed while node still on wrong CPU's list
5. Later RT task triggers balance_callback -> iterates freed node -> UAF panic

Also fix rt.c (demotion) for consistency, though it was technically
safe there since update_curr_rt always runs on the current CPU.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 5 ++++-
 kernel/sched/rt.c   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index ae82906ba..fa46dee33 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -7445,8 +7445,11 @@ enqueue_task_fair(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *p, int flags)
 		    p->infinity.rt_ema < INFINITY_RT_RESTORE_WATERMARK &&
 		    !test_bit(INFINITY_RT_RESTORE_PENDING, &p->infinity.flags)) {
 			set_bit(INFINITY_RT_RESTORE_PENDING, &p->infinity.flags);
+			/* llist_add target must match cpu_of(rq) — during a
+			 * cross-CPU wakeup the current CPU (this_cpu_ptr)
+			 * may differ from the target runqueue's CPU. */
 			if (llist_add(&p->infinity.restore_node,
-				      this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_rt_restore_list))) {
+				      &per_cpu(infinity_rt_restore_list, cpu_of(rq)))) {
 				queue_balance_callback(rq,
 					&per_cpu(infinity_rt_restore_cb, cpu_of(rq)),
 					infinity_rt_restore_worker);
diff --git a/kernel/sched/rt.c b/kernel/sched/rt.c
index 33bb4eaab..cf29548b2 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/rt.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/rt.c
@@ -1003,7 +1003,7 @@ static void update_curr_rt(struct rq *rq)
 		 * Queue the balance_callback only on the first addition to
 		 * avoid redundant callbacks — the worker drains the entire list. */
 		if (llist_add(&donor->infinity.demote_node,
-			      this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_rt_demote_list))) {
+			      &per_cpu(infinity_rt_demote_list, cpu_of(rq)))) {
 			queue_balance_callback(rq,
 				&per_cpu(infinity_rt_demote_cb, cpu_of(rq)),
 				infinity_rt_demote_worker);
-- 
